      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, that's right - it's a slow process. Once the plaque starts leaking, the damaged area of the artery wall becomes more susceptible to inflammation, even with normal amounts of cholesterol. Oxidized LDL (bad) cholesterol is particularly problematic, and when it gets into the artery wall, it can trigger a chain reaction of events, including the production of reactive oxygen species, inflammation, and even the activation of immune cells.",
